node_modules/
# Both forms, and the second is not redundant: the trailing slash matches
# DIRECTORIES ONLY, while the ticket loop plants node_modules as a SYMLINK into
# each worktree (session-manager.js `_runTicketSuite`). Measured on git 2.52.0 —
# with only the slashed form, `git status --porcelain` in such a worktree prints
# `?? node_modules`, which git-worktree.js `isDirty` reads as work to preserve
# and team-retire --discard then silently downgrades to an archive.
node_modules
dist/
# web-dist/ is TRACKED (T42): the prebuilt browser bundle ships in the repo so
# `npm ci --omit=dev` + `git clone` delivers the web GUI to a node with no build
# step. scripts/release.sh runs `npm run build:web` in preflight so a stale
# bundle dirties the tree and fails the release (the staleness guard).
.DS_Store
*.log
.claude/
HANDOFF.local.md
# personal infra (ingress/tunnel manifests) — generic Clodex just serves 7900
deploy/
# …but the clodexctl package's copy of the deploy script MUST ship (npm can't
# reach ../peering); a drift test pins it byte-equal to peering/clodex-deploy.sh.
!cli/deploy/
!cli/deploy/clodex-deploy.sh
!cli/deploy/clodex-fargate.yaml

# Python droppings from running/import-checking the vendored wirescope in place
__pycache__/
vendor/wirescope/warmth.sqlite*

# local design scratch (T44 etc.) — review protocol never commits docs/design/
docs/design/
plugin-context.md
plugin-context.lean.md
.test-digest.lock/

# Team task artifacts. These live in ~/.clodex/projects/<leaf>-<hash>/tasks/
# now (clodex-paths.taskDirFor) — Clodex never writes a user project file, and
# this repo is a product other people clone. Local strays stay unpublished.
tasks/

# Agent artifacts stranded at the REPO ROOT by a spec that named a bare filename
# instead of a path under the task dir. Happened once: an 88-line JOURNAL.md
# shipped into this repo and was caught in review, not by this file. Anchored to
# the root ON PURPOSE — an unanchored NOTES.md would swallow
# plugins/git-branches/NOTES.md and any future docs/SPEC.md. If you legitimately
# want one of these at the root, `git add -f` it; it is ignored here by design,
# not missing.
/JOURNAL.md
/SPEC.md
/NOTES.md
/PLAN.md
/COST.json
